---
// Four terms, four rows. The facts are design.md's: a direct path first, rendezvous for signalling
// only, a relay you run for the rest, and no fallback to a relay nobody named.
---

<section class="section" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="plate">
            <div class="section-grid">
                <div class="section-side">
                    <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="section-main">
                    <p class="section-lede">
                        Two computers, one path, and two servers that only help them meet. A direct
                        transfer sends no bytes through a relay.
                    </p>

                    <dl class="how">
                        <div class="how-row">
                            <dt>Direct path</dt>
                            <dd>
                                Tried first: local discovery, port mapping and hole punching over
                                QUIC. Only the two ends hold the file.
                            </dd>
                        </div>
                        <div class="how-row">
                            <dt>Rendezvous</dt>
                            <dd>
                                A small server you run that answers one question: what is this
                                computer's public address? It carries no file bytes, so the smallest
                                VPS is enough.
                            </dd>
                        </div>
                        <div class="how-row">
                            <dt>Relay</dt>
                            <dd>
                                A server you run that carries the whole transfer when hole punching
                                fails. The image starts closed and relays only the endpoint ids you
                                list.
                            </dd>
                        </div>
                        <div class="how-row">
                            <dt>No relay, no fallback</dt>
                            <dd>
                                n0's public relays and DNS discovery are off. Until you name a relay,
                                Sluice has none. A transfer that cannot go direct fails instead of
                                going somewhere else.
                            </dd>
                        </div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
